  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compare the maximum probabilities of the lotteries and choose the one with the higher maximum probability. The individual does not reference maximum probabilities at all. Instead, their reasoning is based on expected value (which they correctly calculate as equal) and a preference for avoiding loss. This aligns with risk aversion or a focus on downside risk, not the maximum probability rule. While both the decision reason and the individual’s justification lead to the same choice (Lottery A), the underlying logic differs. The individual did not use the maximum probability as a criterion. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
